# Keyword merge (generated by ai_lab/build_keyword_merged.py; sources unchanged). One row per keyword: user reference summary, CR rule number,
# reminder text (printed, else Scryfall fill, else first CR subrule; see reminder_source), first release. Read this file or `python3 tools/agents/lookup.py kw <name>`.
# Full CR rule text is NOT here: it is in KEYWORD_CR_FULLTEXT.toon, which is not to be read unless absolutely needed.
keywords[303]{name,kind,cr_rule,example,summary,reminder,reminder_source,first_release,cards_with}:
  Activate,action,701.2,,,"To activate an activated ability is to put it onto the stack and pay its costs, so that it will eventually resolve and have its effect. Only an object's controller (or its owner, if it doesn't have a controller) can activate its activated ability unless the object specifically says otherwise. A play",cr_subrule_a,,
  Attach,action,701.3,,"Used on auras, equipment, and fortifications (only one fortification, Darksteel Garrison, in the game.) Used to ""put on"" an aura or equipment to a permanent.","To attach an Aura, Equipment, or Fortification to an object or player means to take it from where it currently is and put it onto that object or player. If something is attached to a permanent on the battlefield, it's customary to place it so that it's physically touching the permanent. An Aura, Equ",cr_subrule_a,,
  Behold,action,701.4,,,"""Behold a [quality]"" means ""Reveal a [quality] card from your hand or choose a [quality] permanent you control on the battlefield.""",cr_subrule_a,,
  Cast,action,701.5,,,"To cast a spell is to take it from the zone it's in (usually the hand), put it on the stack, and pay its costs, so that it will eventually resolve and have its effect. A player may cast a spell if they have priority. See rule 601, ""Casting Spells.""",cr_subrule_a,,
  Counter,action,701.6,Counterspell,"Countering a spell or ability removes it from the stack. Also called permission, because you get to say ""no"" to so many things.","To counter a spell or ability means to cancel it, removing it from the stack. It doesn't resolve and none of its effects occur. A countered spell is put into its owner's graveyard.",cr_subrule_a,,
  Create,action,701.7,701.7,"To create one or more tokens with certain characteristics, put the specified number of tokens with the specified characteristics onto the battlefield.","To create one or more tokens with certain characteristics, put the specified number of tokens with the specified characteristics onto the battlefield.",cr_rule_701.7a,,
  Destroy,action,701.8,701.8,"To destroy a permanent, move it from the battlefield to its owner's graveyard.","To destroy a permanent, move it from the battlefield to its owner's graveyard.",cr_rule_701.8a,,
  Discard,action,701.9,701.9,"To discard a card, move it from its owner's hand to that player's graveyard.","To discard a card, move it from its owner's hand to that player's graveyard.",cr_rule_701.9a,,
  Double,action,701.10,701.10,Doubling a creature's power and/or toughness creates a continuous effect. This effect modifies that creature's power and/or toughness but doesn't set those characteristics to a specific value. See rule 613.4c.,Doubling a creature's power and/or toughness creates a continuous effect. This effect modifies that creature's power and/or toughness but doesn't set those characteristics to a specific value. See rule 613.4c.,cr_rule_701.10a,,
  Triple,action,701.11,701.11,Tripling a creature's power and/or toughness creates a continuous effect. This effect modifies that creature's power and/or toughness but doesn't set those characteristics to a specific value. See rule 613.4c.,Tripling a creature's power and/or toughness creates a continuous effect. This effect modifies that creature's power and/or toughness but doesn't set those characteristics to a specific value. See rule 613.4c.,cr_rule_701.11a,,
  Exchange,action,701.12,701.12,"A spell or ability may instruct players to exchange something (for example, life totals or control of two permanents) as part of its resolution. When such a spell or ability resolves, if the entire exchange can't be completed, no part of the exchange occurs. Example: If a spell attempts to exchange","A spell or ability may instruct players to exchange something (for example, life totals or control of two permanents) as part of its resolution. When such a spell or ability resolves, if the entire exchange can't be completed, no part of the exchange occurs. Example: If a spell attempts to exchange control of two target creatures but one of those creatures is destroyed before the spell resolves, the spell does nothin",cr_rule_701.12a,,
  Exile,action,701.13,701.13,"To exile an object, move it to the exile zone from wherever it is. See rule 406, ""Exile.""","To exile an object, move it to the exile zone from wherever it is. See rule 406, ""Exile.""",cr_rule_701.13a,,
  Fight,action,701.14,701.14,A spell or ability may instruct a creature to fight another creature or it may instruct two creatures to fight each other. Each of those creatures deals damage equal to its power to the other creature.,Each deals damage equal to its power to the other.,scryfall_api,,
  Goad,action,701.15,701.15,"Certain spells and abilities can goad a creature. Until the next turn of the controller of that spell or ability, that creature is goaded.","Until your next turn, that creature attacks each combat if able and attacks a player other than you if able.",scryfall_api,,
  Investigate,keyword,701.16,Thraben Inspector,"Whenever a card investigates, create a clue tokens. Clue tokens have ""Pay 2 mana and sacrifice this artifact, draw a card.""","Create a Clue token. It's an artifact with ""{N}, Sacrifice this token: Draw a card.""",scryfall_api,2016-04-08,147
  Mill,action,701.17,701.17,"For a player to mill a number of cards, that player puts that many cards from the top of their library into their graveyard.","For a player to mill a number of cards, that player puts that many cards from the top of their library into their graveyard.",cr_rule_701.17a,,
  Play,action,701.18,701.18,"To play a land means to put it onto the battlefield from the zone it's in (usually the hand). A player may play a land if they have priority, it's the main phase of their turn, the stack is empty, and they haven't played a land this turn. Playing a land is a special action (see rule 116), so it does","To play a land means to put it onto the battlefield from the zone it's in (usually the hand). A player may play a land if they have priority, it's the main phase of their turn, the stack is empty, and they haven't played a land this turn. Playing a land is a special action (see rule 116), so it doesn't use the stack; it simply happens. Putting a land onto the battlefield as the result of a spell or ability isn't the",cr_rule_701.18a,,
  Regenerate,action,701.19,,,"If the effect of a resolving spell or ability regenerates a permanent, it creates a replacement effect that protects the permanent the next time it would be destroyed this turn. In this case, ""Regenerate [permanent]"" means ""The next time [permanent] would be destroyed this turn, instead remove all d",cr_subrule_a,,
  Reveal,action,701.20,701.20,"To reveal a card, show that card to all players for a brief time. If an effect causes a card to be revealed, it remains revealed for as long as necessary to complete the parts of the effect that card is relevant to. If the cost to cast a spell or activate an ability includes revealing a card, or if","To reveal a card, show that card to all players for a brief time. If an effect causes a card to be revealed, it remains revealed for as long as necessary to complete the parts of the effect that card is relevant to. If the cost to cast a spell or activate an ability includes revealing a card, or if a card is revealed because an ability is activated from a hidden zone (see rule 602.2a), the card remains revealed from",cr_rule_701.20a,,
  Sacrifice,action,701.21,Chainer's Edict,"The owner of a permanent places it into their own graveyard due to an effect or spell. Some spells cause you to sacrifice a creature as an additional cost, sometimes spells an opponent cast can cause you to sacrifice a creature.","To sacrifice a permanent, its controller moves it from the battlefield directly to its owner's graveyard. A player can't sacrifice something that isn't a permanent, or something that's a permanent they don't control. Sacrificing a permanent doesn't destroy it, so regeneration or other effects that replace destruction can't affect this action.",cr_rule_701.21a,,
  Scry,action,701.22,Crystal Ball,"Written as ""Scry X"" where X is a number Look at the top X cards of your library, put any number on the bottom of your library. Put the rest back in any order.",Look at the top card of your library. You may put that card on the bottom.,scryfall_api,2004-02-06,454
  Search,action,701.23,701.23,"To search for a card in a zone, look at all cards in that zone (even if it's a hidden zone) and find a card that matches the given description.","To search for a card in a zone, look at all cards in that zone (even if it's a hidden zone) and find a card that matches the given description.",cr_rule_701.23a,,
  Shuffle,action,701.24,701.24,"To shuffle a library or a face-down pile of cards, randomize the cards within it so that no player knows their order.","To shuffle a library or a face-down pile of cards, randomize the cards within it so that no player knows their order.",cr_rule_701.24a,,
  Surveil,keyword,701.25,Notion Rain,"Written as ""Surveil X"", where X is a number When the ability resolves, look at the top X cards of your library. You may put any number into your graveyard and rest back on top of your library in any order.","Look at the top two cards of your library, then put any number of them into your graveyard and the rest on top of your library in any order.",forge_oracle,2001-10-01,263
  Tap and Untap,action,701.26,,,"To tap a permanent, turn it sideways from an upright position. Only untapped permanents can be tapped.",cr_rule_701.26a,,
  Transform,keyword,701.27,Aberrant Researcher // Perfected Form,"Applies to double-faced cards. When some condition is met, you may transform a card from its front side to its back side. What causes a transformation varies widely from in-game actions to mana costs.","If a player casts no spells during their own turn, it becomes night next turn.",scryfall_api,2011-09-30,437
  Convert,action,701.28,,,"To convert a permanent, turn it so that its other face is up. This follows rules 701.27a-f, 712.9-10, and 712.18. Those rules apply to converting a permanent just as they apply to transforming a permanent.",cr_subrule_a,,
  Fateseal,keyword,701.29,Spin into myth,"When you ""scry"" on your opponents' library. You are allowed to look at the top X cards of the opponent's library, as dictated by the number in the keyword. You then decide what stays on top of the library and what goes to the bottom.","To fateseal N, its controller looks at the top card of an opponent's library, then they may put that card on the bottom of that library.",scryfall_api,2007-05-04,3
  Clash,action,701.30,Fire Juggler,"When a spell tells players to clash, each player reveals the top card of their library. When they do, the person with the higher mana value of the revealed card wins the clash. In the event of a tie, there is no winner.","Each clashing player reveals the top card of their library, then puts that card on their choice of the top or bottom. A player wins if their card had a greater mana value.",scryfall_api,2007-10-12,29
  Planeswalk,action,701.31,701.31,"A player may planeswalk only during a Planechase game. Only the planar controller may planeswalk. See rule 901, ""Planechase.""","A player may planeswalk only during a Planechase game. Only the planar controller may planeswalk. See rule 901, ""Planechase.""",cr_rule_701.31a,,
  Set in Motion,action,701.32,701.32,"Only a scheme card may be set in motion, and only during an Archenemy game. Only the archenemy may set a scheme card in motion. See rule 314, ""Schemes,"" and rule 904, ""Archenemy.""","Only a scheme card may be set in motion, and only during an Archenemy game. Only the archenemy may set a scheme card in motion. See rule 314, ""Schemes,"" and rule 904, ""Archenemy.""",cr_rule_701.32a,,
  Abandon,action,701.33,701.33,"Only a face-up ongoing scheme card may be abandoned, and only during an Archenemy game. See rule 314, ""Schemes,"" and rule 904, ""Archenemy.""","Only a face-up ongoing scheme card may be abandoned, and only during an Archenemy game. See rule 314, ""Schemes,"" and rule 904, ""Archenemy.""",cr_rule_701.33a,,
  Proliferate,keyword,701.34,Grateful Apparition,"Whenever you proliferate, you may add an additional counter to anything that already has a counter. This includes +1/+1 counters, loyalty counters, poison counters, etc. Basically all counters.","Choose any number of permanents and/or players, then give each another counter of each kind already there.",scryfall_api,2010-10-01,106
  Detain,keyword,701.35,Lavinia of the Tenth,"Whenever a player ""detains"" a permanent, that permanent cannot attack, block, or activate abilities until the start of that player's next turn.","Until your next turn, that creature can't attack or block and its activated abilities can't be activated.",scryfall_api,2012-10-05,14
  Populate,keyword,701.36,Growing Ranks,Make a copy of a creature token you control.,Create a token that's a copy of a creature token you control.,scryfall_api,2012-10-05,27
  Monstrosity,keyword,701.37,Fleecemane Lion,"Written as ""[cost]: Monstrosity X"", where X is a number As long as a card has not already become monstrous, you may pay the monstrosity cost and put X +1/+1 counters on that creature.","If this creature isn't monstrous, put three +N/+N counters on it and it becomes monstrous.",scryfall_api,2013-09-27,37
  Vote,action,701.38,701.38,"Some spells and abilities instruct players to vote for one choice from a list of options to determine some aspect of the effect of that spell or ability. To vote, each player, starting with a specified player and proceeding in turn order, chooses one of those choices.","Some spells and abilities instruct players to vote for one choice from a list of options to determine some aspect of the effect of that spell or ability. To vote, each player, starting with a specified player and proceeding in turn order, chooses one of those choices.",cr_rule_701.38a,,
  Bolster,keyword,701.39,"Dromoka, the Eternal","Written as ""Bolster X"", where X is a number Whenever a creature with bolster attacks, you put X +1/+1 counters on target creature you control with the lowest toughness equal to the X in bolster.",Choose a creature with the least toughness among creatures you control and put a +N/+N counter on it.,scryfall_api,2015-01-23,25
  Manifest,keyword,701.40,Reality Shift,"Written as ""Manifest [one or more cards]"" Manifested cards are face-down 2/2 creatures, just like morphs. Manifested creatures may be turned face up for their mana cost.",Look at the top two cards of your library. Put one onto the battlefield face down as a N/N creature and the other into your graveyard. Turn it face up any time for its mana cost if it's a creature card.,scryfall_api,2015-01-23,68
  Support,keyword,701.41,Generous Patron,"Written as ""Support X"", where X is a number When the ability resolves, place a +1/+1 counter on up to X target creatures.",Put a +N/+N counter on each of up to two target creatures.,scryfall_api,2016-01-22,20
  Meld,keyword,701.42,"Brisela, Voice of Nightmares","2 cards can be melded together to create a single creature. Only in one set, not many cards.","Meld is a keyword action that appears in an ability on one card in a meld pair. To meld the two cards in a meld pair, put them onto the battlefield with their back faces up and combined. The resulting permanent is a single object represented by two cards. See rule 712, ""Double- Faced Cards.""",cr_rule_701.42a,2022-11-18,7
  Exert,keyword,701.43,Glorybringer,"When a creature with exert attacks, you may ""exert"" the card. If you do, it does not untap during its controller's next untap step. Cards grant some ability when you exert them.",An exerted creature won't untap during your next untap step.,scryfall_api,2017-04-28,36
  Explore,keyword,701.44,Merfolk Branchwalker,"Whenever a creature with explore enters the battlefield, reveal the top card of your library. If it is a land card, put it into your hand. If it is a nonland card, you may put it into your graveyard. For each nonland card revealed this way, put a +1/+1 counter","Reveal the top card of your library. Put that card into your hand if it's a land. Otherwise, put a +N/+N counter on this creature, then put the card back or put it into your graveyard.",scryfall_api,2017-09-29,59
  Assemble,action,701.45,701.45,"Assemble is a keyword action in the Unstable set that puts Contraptions onto the battlefield. Outside of silver-bordered cards, only one card (Steamflogger Boss) refers to assembling a Contraption. Cards and mechanics from the Unstable set aren't included in these rules. See the Unstable FAQ for mor",Put the top card of your Contraption deck face up onto one of your sprockets.,scryfall_api,,
  Adapt,keyword,701.46,Growth-Chamber Guardian,"Written as ""[cost] Adapt X"", where X is a number When the adapt cost is paid, put X +1/+1 counters on the creatures whose ability was activated.","If this creature has no +N/+N counters on it, put two +N/+N counters on it.",scryfall_api,2019-01-25,25
  Amass,action,701.47,701.47,"To amass [subtype] N means ""If you don't control an Army creature, create a 0/0 black [subtype] Army creature token. Choose an Army creature you control. Put N +1/+1 counters on that creature. If it isn't a [subtype], it becomes a [subtype] in addition to its other types.""","Put a +N/+N counter on an Army you control. It's also a Zombie. If you don't control an Army, create a N/N black Zombie Army creature token first.",scryfall_api,,
  Learn,action,701.48,701.48,"""Learn"" means ""You may discard a card. If you do, draw a card. If you didn't discard a card, you may reveal a Lesson card you own from outside the game and put it into your hand.""","You may reveal a Lesson card you own from outside the game and put it into your hand, or discard a card to draw a card.",scryfall_api,,
  Venture into the Dungeon,action,701.49,701.49,"If a player is instructed to venture into the dungeon while they don't own a dungeon card in the command zone, they choose a dungeon card they own from outside the game and put it into the command zone. They put their venture marker on the topmost room. See rule 309, ""Dungeons.""",Enter the first room or advance to the next room.,scryfall_api,,
  Connive,keyword,701.50,Ledger Shredder,"Written as ""[CARDNAME] connives"" Whenever a card connives, you draw and discard a card. If a nonland card was discarded this way, put a +1/+1 counter on the creature that connived.","Draw a card, then discard a card. If you discarded a nonland card, put a +N/+N counter on this creature.",scryfall_api,2022-04-29,51
  Open an Attraction,action,701.51,701.51,"A player may open an Attraction only during a game in which that player is playing with an Attraction deck (see rule 717, ""Attraction Cards"").",Put the top card of your Attraction deck onto the battlefield.,scryfall_api,,
  Roll to Visit Your Attractions,action,701.52,701.52,"To roll to visit your Attractions, roll a six-sided die. Then if you control one or more Attractions with a number lit up that is equal to that result, each of those Attractions has been ""visited"" and its visit ability triggers. See rule 717, ""Attraction Cards,"" and rule 702.159, ""Visit.""",Put the top card of your Attraction deck onto the battlefield.,scryfall_api,,
  Incubate,action,701.53,701.53,"To incubate N, create an Incubator token that enters the battlefield with N +1/+1 counters on it. See rule 111.10i.","Create an Incubator token with two +N/+N counters on it and ""{N}: Transform this token."" It transforms into a N/N Phyrexian artifact creature.",scryfall_api,,
  The Ring Tempts You,action,701.54,701.54,"Certain spells and abilities have the text ""the Ring tempts you."" Each time the Ring tempts you, choose a creature you control. That creature becomes your Ring-bearer until another creature becomes your Ring-bearer or another player gains control of it.","Certain spells and abilities have the text ""the Ring tempts you."" Each time the Ring tempts you, choose a creature you control. That creature becomes your Ring-bearer until another creature becomes your Ring-bearer or another player gains control of it.",cr_rule_701.54a,,
  Face a Villainous Choice,action,701.55,701.55,"""[A player] faces a villainous choice — [option A], or [option B]"" means ""[A player] chooses [option A] or [option B]. Then all actions in the chosen option are performed.""","""[A player] faces a villainous choice - [option A], or [option B]"" means ""[A player] chooses [option A] or [option B]. Then all actions in the chosen option are performed.""",cr_rule_701.55a,,
  Time Travel,action,701.56,,,"To time travel means to choose any number of permanents you control with one or more time counters on them and/or suspended cards you own in exile with one or more time counters on them and, for each of those objects, put a time counter on it or remove a time counter from it. See rule 702.62, ""Suspe",cr_subrule_a,,
  Discover,action,701.57,701.57,"""Discover N"" means ""Exile cards from the top of your library until you exile a nonland card with mana value N or less. You may cast that card without paying its mana cost if the resulting spell's mana value is less than or equal to N. If you don't cast it, put that card into your hand. Put the remai",Exile cards from the top of your library until you exile a nonland card with mana value N or less. Cast it without paying its mana cost or put it into your hand. Put the rest on the bottom in a random order.,scryfall_api,,
  Cloak,action,701.58,701.58,"To cloak a card, turn it face down. It becomes a 2/2 face-down creature card with ward {2}, no name, no subtypes, and no mana cost. Put that card onto the battlefield face down. That permanent is a cloaked permanent for as long as it remains face down. The effect defining its characteristics works w","To cloak a card, put it onto the battlefield face down as a N/N creature with ward {N}. Turn it face up any time for its mana cost if it's a creature card.",scryfall_api,,
  Collect Evidence,action,701.59,,,"To ""collect evidence N"" means to exile any number of cards from your graveyard with total mana value N or greater.",cr_subrule_a,,
  Suspect,action,701.60,701.60,Certain spells and abilities instruct a player to suspect a creature. That creature becomes suspected until it leaves the battlefield or until a spell or ability causes it to no longer be suspected.,A suspected creature has menace and can't block.,scryfall_api,,
  Forage,action,701.61,701.61,"To forage means ""Exile three cards from your graveyard or sacrifice a Food.""","To forage, exile three cards from your graveyard or sacrifice a Food.",scryfall_api,,
  Manifest Dread,action,701.62,701.62,"""Manifest dread"" means ""Look at the top two cards of your library. Manifest one of them, then put the cards you looked at that were not manifested this way into your graveyard."" See rule 701.40, ""Manifest.""",Look at the top two cards of your library. Put one onto the battlefield face down as a N/N creature and the other into your graveyard. Turn it face up any time for its mana cost if it's a creature card.,scryfall_api,,
  Endure,action,701.63,701.63,"Certain abilities instruct a permanent to endure N. To do so, that permanent's controller creates an N/N white Spirit creature token unless they put N +1/+1 counters on that permanent.",Put a +N/+N counter on it or create a N/N white Spirit creature token.,scryfall_api,,
  Harness,action,701.64,701.64,"""Harness [this permanent]"" means ""If this permanent isn't harnessed, it becomes harnessed.""","""Harness [this permanent]"" means ""If this permanent isn't harnessed, it becomes harnessed.""",cr_rule_701.64a,,
  Airbend,action,701.65,701.65,"Certain spells and abilities instruct a player to airbend one or more permanents and/or spells. To do so, that player exiles those objects. For each card exiled this way, for as long as it remains exiled, its owner may cast it by paying {2} rather than paying its mana cost.","Exile it. While it's exiled, its owner may cast it for {N} rather than its mana cost.",scryfall_api,,
  Earthbend,action,701.66,701.66,"""Earthbend N"" means ""Target land you control becomes a 0/0 land creature with haste in addition to its other types. Put N +1/+1 counters on it. When that land dies or is put into exile, return it to the battlefield tapped under your control.""","Target land you control becomes a N/N creature with haste that's still a land. Put two +N/+N counters on it. When it dies or is exiled, return it to the battlefield tapped.",scryfall_api,,
  Waterbend,action,701.67,701.67,"""Waterbend [cost]"" means ""Pay [cost]. For each generic mana in that cost, you may tap an untapped artifact or creature you control rather than pay that mana.""","While paying a waterbend cost, you can tap your artifacts and creatures to help. Each one pays for {N}.",scryfall_api,,
  Blight,action,701.68,701.68,"To ""blight N"" means to put N -1/-1 counters on a creature you control.","To blight N, put a -N/-N counter on a creature you control.",scryfall_api,,
  Heal,action,701.69,701.69,"To heal damage already dealt to a permanent, remove that marked damage from that permanent. If an effect states that damage already dealt to a permanent ""is healed,"" that permanent's controller removes all marked damage from that permanent.","The next time this creature would be destroyed this turn, instead tap it, remove it from combat, and heal all damage on it.",scryfall_api,,
  Recruit,action,701.70,,,"""Recruit"" means ""Draw a card, then discard a card. If you discarded a nonland card this way, create a 1/1 white Human Soldier creature token.""",cr_subrule_a,,
  Deathtouch,keyword,702.2,Sedge Scorpion,"Whenever a creature with deathtouch deals damage to another creature, that creature will die. It does not have to be combat damage, so if you have a card like Rabid Bite, it will still kill the creature dealt damage.",Any amount of damage this deals to a creature is enough to destroy it.,forge_oracle,2007-10-12,364
  Defender,keyword,702.3,Wall of Mist,"Creature cannot attack. In the past, there was a rule that said ""Walls can't attack."" So if you see an old creature with the type ""Wall"", but it doesn't have defender in the text-box, it still has defender.",This creature can't attack.,printed,1994-06-01,315
  Double Strike,keyword,702.4,Boros Swiftblade,Creature deals both first strike damage and regular damage.,This creature deals both first-strike and regular combat damage.,printed,2003-02-03,134
  Enchant,keyword,702.5,Abundant Growth,"Written as ""Enchant X"" where X is a permanent type These are auras.",Target a creature as you cast this. This card enters attached to that creature.,printed,1994-03-04,1279
  Equip,keyword,702.6,Sword of Feast and Famine,"Written as ""Equip X"" where X is a mana cost These are equipment.",{N}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery.,forge_oracle,2003-10-02,632
  First Strike,keyword,702.7,Battle Hurda,"Creature with first strike deals damage before creatures without first strike in combat. For example, if you have a 2/2 elf and a 2/2 soldier with first strike in combat, the elf would die before it deals damage to the soldier.",This creature deals combat damage before creatures without first strike.,printed,1993-12-17,408
  Flash,keyword,702.8,Bounding Krasis,"This is on nonland permanent cards (creatures, artifact, enchantments, planeswalkers). Permits you to cast those spells whenever you could cast an instant.",You may cast this spell any time you could cast an instant.,printed,1999-02-15,641
  Flying,keyword,702.9,Storm Crow,Creatures with flying can only be blocked by other creatures with flying or by creatures with reach.,This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.,printed,1994-06-01,3366
  Haste,keyword,702.10,Tenement Crasher,"Creatures with haste may attack or activate ""tap"" abilities the turn they come into play, i.e. no summoning sickness.",This creature can attack and {C} as soon as it comes under your control.,printed,1996-06-10,702
  Hexproof,keyword,702.11,Soul of the Rapids,Cannot be the target of spells or abilities an opponent controls. Its controller can still target it.,This creature can't be the target of spells or abilities your opponents control.,printed,,
  Indestructible,keyword,702.12,"Avacyn, Angle of Hope","Creatures with indestructible cannot be removed from the battlefield by effects that say ""destroy"" nor damage. You can remove indestructible creatures and permanents by exile effects (Swords to Plowshares), -1/-1 effects (Toxic Deluge), and bounce effects (Cyc","Effects that say ""destroy"" don't destroy this artifact.",printed,2004-02-06,116
  Intimidate,keyword,702.13,,,Intimidate is an evasion ability.,cr_subrule_a,,
  Landwalk,keyword,702.14,Benthic Behemoth,"Written as ""plainswalk"" or ""islandwalk"",etc Creatures with landwalk cannot be blocked if the defending player has a land that is the type mentioned in the ability.",This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a land of that type.,forge_oracle,1993-12-17,133
  Lifelink,keyword,702.15,Bishop's Soldier,"Whenever a creature with lifelink deals damage, either to an opponent or creature, you gain life equal to the amount of damage. All damage happens at the same time. If you are dealt lethal damage, but have a lifelink creature to block that brings you back up a",Damage dealt by this creature also causes you to gain that much life.,printed,2007-10-12,404
  Protection,keyword,702.16,Apostle of Purifying Light,"Written as ""Protection from X"" This is complicated.","This creature can't be blocked, targeted, dealt damage, or enchanted by anything white.",printed,1994-06-01,209
  Reach,keyword,702.17,Giant Spider,Creatures with reach may block creatures with flying.,This creature can block creatures with flying.,printed,1995-10-01,450
  Shroud,keyword,702.18,Argothian Enchantress,Creatures with shroud cannot be the target of spells or abilities. That includes all players.,This creature can't be the target of spells or abilities.,printed,1996-10-08,39
  Trample,keyword,702.19,Colossal Dreadmaw,Creatures with trample deal excess damage to defending player. Example,This creature can deal excess combat damage to the player or planeswalker it's attacking.,printed,1994-08-01,1059
  Vigilance,keyword,702.20,Serra Angel,Attacking does not cause creature to tap.,Attacking doesn't cause this creature to tap.,printed,1995-10-01,775
  Ward,keyword,702.21,Dreadlight Monstrosity,"Written as ""Ward [cost]"" If a creature with ward becomes the target of a spell or ability an opponent controls, counter that spell unless the opponent pays the ward cost.","Whenever this creature becomes the target of a spell or ability an opponent controls, counter it unless that player pays {C}.",printed,2021-04-23,216
  Banding,keyword,702.22,Knights of Thorn,"Historically, THE MOST complicated mechanic in all of MTG history. 53 words of rules text:","Any creatures with banding, and up to one without, can attack in a band. Bands are blocked as a group. If any creatures with banding you control are blocking or being blocked by a creature, you divide that creature's combat damage, not its controller, among any of the creatures it's being blocked by or is blocking.",printed,1993-12-17,26
  Rampage,keyword,702.23,Craw Giant,"Written as ""Rampage X"", where X is a number. Whenever a creature with rampage is blocked, it gets +X/+X until end of turn for each creature blocking it.","Whenever this creature becomes blocked, it gets +N/+N until end of turn for each creature blocking it beyond the first.",printed,1994-06-01,15
  Cumulative Upkeep,keyword,702.24,Mystic Remora,"Written as ""Cumulative Upkeep [cost]"" Old and difficult mechanic. Essentially, the cost compounds each turn, and must be paid at the upkeep step. On your upkeep you place an age-counter on the card with cumulative upkeep, then pay the upkeep cost as many times","At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.",forge_oracle,1995-06-03,82
  Flanking,keyword,702.25,Benalish Cavalry,"Whenever a creature with flanking is blocked, the blocking creature gets -1/-1 until the end of the turn. Older mechanic; rare and not all that good.","Whenever a creature without flanking blocks this creature, the blocking creature gets -N/-N until end of turn.",printed,1996-10-08,30
  Phasing,keyword,702.26,Sandbar Crocodile,"Old and complicated mechanic Cards that are phased out are treated as though they don't exist. Any auras and equipment attached do not fall off and are phased out with the creature. It's similar to exile, but the creatures return at the beginning of their cont","This phases in or out before you untap during each of your untap steps. While it's phased out, it's treated as though it doesn't exist.",printed,1996-10-08,13
  Buyback,keyword,702.27,Capsize,"Written as ""Buyback X"", where X is a mana cost. Only on instants and sorceries. When you cast a card, you may pay the buyback cost. If you do, instead of the card going to your graveyard, it goes back to your hand after resolving.","You may pay an additional {C} as you cast this spell. If you do, put this card into your hand as it resolves.",printed,1997-10-14,41
  Shadow,keyword,702.28,Dauthi Cutthroat,Creatures with shadow can only block or be blocked by other creatures with shadow.,This creature can block or be blocked by only creatures with shadow.,printed,1997-10-14,40
  Cycling,keyword,702.29,Cast Out,"Written as ""Cycling [cost] Whenever a card has cycling, you may pay the cycling cost and discard that card. Then you draw a new card.","{C}, Discard this card: Draw a card.",printed,1998-10-12,410
  Echo,keyword,702.30,Avalanche Riders,"Written as ""Echo [cost]"" Whenever a card with echo comes into play under your control, you must pay the echo cost at the beginning of the next upkeep or sacrifice the creature.","At the beginning of your upkeep, if this came under your control since the beginning of your last upkeep, sacrifice it unless you pay its echo cost.",printed,1998-10-12,52
  Horsemanship,keyword,702.31,"Sun Quan, Lord of Wu","Horsemanship is like flying. Creatures with horsemanship can't be blocked by creatures without horsemanship, unless explicitly stated otherwise. Only from an old set called Portal: 3 Kingdoms. Set in the 3 Kingdoms era in China. Was originally meant to try to",This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with horsemanship.,printed,1999-05-01,30
  Fading,keyword,702.32,Tangle Wire,"Written as ""Fading X"", where X is a number Cards with fading enter the battlefield with X fading counters on them. At the beginning of your upkeep, remove a fading counter from that permanent. If you cannot remove a fading counter, sacrifice that creature.","This creature enters with three fade counters on it. At the beginning of your upkeep, remove a fade counter from it. If you can't, sacrifice it.",printed,2000-02-14,18
  Kicker,keyword,702.33,"Tourach, Dread Cantor","Written as ""Kicker [cost]"" When you cast a spell, you may also pay the kicker cost to have an additional effect happen.",You may pay an additional {C}{C} as you cast this spell.,printed,2000-10-02,236
  Flashback,keyword,702.34,Faithless Looting,"Written as ""Flashback [cost]"" When a card with flashback is in the graveyard, you may cast it for its flashback cost, then exile it.",You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.,printed,2001-10-01,219
  Madness,keyword,702.35,Basking Rootwalla,"Written as ""Madness [cost]"" When a spell with madness is discarded, it is exiled. Then, you may cast that card for it's madness cost. If you don't cast it, it is then moved to the graveyard.","If you discard this card, discard it into exile. When you do, cast it for its madness cost or put it into your graveyard.",printed,2002-02-04,63
  Fear,keyword,702.36,Dross Prowler,Only on black cards. The creature that has fear cannot be blocked except by black and artifact creatures.,This creature can't be blocked except by artifact creatures and/or black creatures.,printed,1997-02-03,40
  Morph,keyword,702.37,Blistering Firecat,,You may cast this card face down as a N/N creature for {C}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.,printed,,
  Amplify,keyword,702.38,Kilnmouth Dragon,"Written as ""Amplify X"", where X is a number When you cast a card with amplify, you may reveal any number of cards that share a card type with that card. The card that was cast then enters with a number of +1/+1 counters equal to X times the amount of cards rev","As this creature enters, put a +N/+N counter on it for each Zombie card you reveal in your hand.",printed,2003-02-03,9
  Provoke,keyword,702.39,Lowland Tracker,"When a creature with provoke attacks, its controller may target a creature defending player controls. Then, untap that creature (if applicable). That creature must block the attacking creature with provoke. They mostly suck in general.","Whenever this creature attacks, you may have target creature defending player controls untap and block it if able.",printed,2003-02-03,9
  Storm,keyword,702.40,Grapeshot,"Whenever a card with storm is cast, copy it for each spell cast before it this turn. For example, if you cast 2 lightning bolts and then a Grapeshot, there are actually 3 copies of grapeshot because it is copied 2 times from the 2 lightning bolts cast before i","When you cast this spell, copy it for each spell cast before it this turn.",printed,2003-05-26,40
  Affinity,keyword,702.41,Thoughtcast,"Written as ""Affinity for X"", where X is a card type Most commonly written as ""affinity for artifacts"", a card can have affinity for anything.",This spell costs {C} less to cast for each artifact you control.,printed,2003-10-02,78
  Entwine,keyword,702.42,Tooth and Nail,"Written as ""Entwine [cost]"" On cards with 2 options, it allows you to pay mana in addition to the casting cost to do both options.",Choose both if you pay the entwine cost.,printed,2003-10-02,33
  Modular,keyword,702.43,Arcbound Mouser,"Written as ""Modular X"", where X is a number Creatures with modular enter with X +1/+1 counters. When a creature with modular dies, it's counters may be moved to another target artifact creature.","This creature enters with two +N/+N counters on it. When it dies, you may put its +N/+N counters on target artifact creature.",printed,2004-02-06,24
  Sunburst,keyword,702.44,Engineered Explosives,"A card with sunburst enters with a counter on it for each color of mana used to cast the spell. If a card with sunburst cost 5 generic mana, and you spend 3 green mana and 2 black mana, it only gets 2 counters. If you spend one of every color of mana, it gets",This enters with a +N/+N counter on it for each color of mana spent to cast it.,printed,2004-06-04,16
  Bushido,keyword,702.45,Devoted Retainer,"Written as ""Bushido X"", where X is a number If a creature with Bushido is blocked or blocks, it gets +X/+X until the end of the turn, where X is the number associated with Bushido.","Whenever this creature blocks or becomes blocked, it gets +N/+N until end of turn.",printed,2004-10-01,38
  Soulshift,keyword,702.46,Elder Pine of Jukai,"Written as ""Soulshift X"", where X is a number Whenever a creature with soulshift is put into the graveyard, its controller may return a spirit card from the graveyard to their hand with mana value X or less.","When this creature dies, you may return target Spirit card with mana value N or less from your graveyard to your hand.",printed,2004-10-01,26
  Splice,keyword,702.47,Everdream,"Written as ""Splice onto X"", where X is a card type When you cast a card of the specified type, you may pay the splice cost and reveal that card. The effect of the revealed card is then ""tacked onto"" the spell being cast.","As you cast an Arcane spell, you may reveal this card from your hand and pay its splice cost. If you do, add this card's effects to that spell.",printed,2004-10-01,32
  Offering,keyword,702.48,Patron of the Kitsune,"Written as ""[creature type] offering"" Creatures with offering may be cast as though it has flash if you sacrifice a creature of the appropriate type. Also, the mana cost is altered based on what you sacrifice. For example, Patron of the Orochi has snake offeri",You may cast this spell as though it had flash by sacrificing an artifact and paying the difference in mana costs between this and the sacrificed artifact. Mana cost includes color.,scryfall_api,2005-02-04,6
  Ninjutsu,keyword,702.49,Ninja of the Deep Hours,"Written as ""Ninjutsu [cost]"" You may return an unblocked attacking creature you control and put a ninja down in its' place, attacking.","{C}{C}, Return an unblocked attacker you control to hand: Put this card onto the battlefield from your hand tapped and attacking.",printed,2016-11-25,37
  Epic,keyword,702.50,Enduring Ideal,"After a card with Epic resolves, you may no longer cast spells. Instead, it provides you with (typically), some insane benefit.","For the rest of the game, you can't cast spells. At the beginning of each of your upkeeps, copy this spell except for its epic ability. You may choose a new target for the copy.",printed,2005-06-03,5
  Convoke,keyword,702.51,March of the Multitudes,"Convoke allows you to tap creatures to pay for the cost in a spell. Creatures tapped with convoke can either pay for generic costs or colored costs, as long as they are the same color as the mana symbol they are paying.",Your creatures can help cast this spell. Each creature you tap while casting this spell pays for {C} or one mana of that creature's color.,printed,2005-10-07,106
  Dredge,keyword,702.52,Life from the Loam,"Written as ""Dredge X"", where X is a number If a card with dredge is in your graveyard, instead of drawing a card, you may put the top X cards of your library into your graveyard where X number associated with the ability, and return the dredge card to your han","If you would draw a card, you may mill two cards instead. If you do, return this card from your graveyard to your hand.",printed,2005-10-07,14
  Transmute,keyword,702.53,Muddle the Mixture,"Written as ""Transmute [cost]"" When you transmute a card, you pay the transmute cost and discard that card, then search your library for a card with the same mana value.","{C}{C}{C}, Discard this card: Search your library for a card with the same mana value as this card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle. Transmute only as a sorcery.",printed,2005-10-07,14
  Bloodthirst,keyword,702.54,Scab-Clan Mauler,"Written as ""Bloodthirst X"", where X is a number Creatures with Bloodthirst counters enter the battlefield with X +1/+1 counters on them, if an opponent was dealt damage this turn.","If an opponent was dealt damage this turn, this creature enters with a +N/+N counter on it.",printed,2006-02-03,23
  Haunt,keyword,702.55,Belfry Spirit,"Once a creature or spell with haunt enters the graveyard, it is exiled and then attached to a creature on the battlefield to ""haunt it"". All cards with the haunt mechanic have an enter the battlefield trigger that is the same as the haunt trigger. The haunt tr","When this creature dies, exile it haunting target creature.",printed,2006-02-03,10
  Replicate,keyword,702.56,Shattering Spree,"Written as ""Replicate [cost]"" Whenever you cast a spell, you may pay its replicate cost any number of times. If you do, copy that spell for each time you paid the replicate cost.","When you cast this spell, copy it for each time you paid its replicate cost. You may choose new targets for the copies.",printed,2006-02-03,21
  Forecast,keyword,702.57,Proclamation of Rebirth,"Written as ""Forecast [cost]"" During your upkeep, you may pay the forecast cost and reveal the forecast card from your hand, then the ability from forecast resolves.","A forecast ability is an activated ability that can be activated only from a player's hand. It's written ""Forecast - [Activated ability].""",cr_rule_702.57a,2006-05-05,12
  Graft,keyword,702.58,Plaxcaster Frogling,"Written as ""Graft X"" where X is a number All creatures with graft are 0/0s that enter the battlefield with X +1/+1 counters on them equal to the graft number. Whenever another creature enters the battlefield, creatures with graft may move one of their counters","This creature enters with two +N/+N counters on it. Whenever another creature enters, you may move a +N/+N counter from this creature onto it.",printed,2006-05-05,13
  Recover,keyword,702.59,Icefall,"Written as ""Recover [cost]"" Whenever a creature is put into a player's graveyard from the battlefield, all cards with recover trigger. You may then pay the recover cost for each card and return it to your hand. If you do not or cannot pay the cost, the card is","When a creature is put into your graveyard from the battlefield, you may pay {C}{C}. If you do, return this card from your graveyard to your hand. Otherwise, exile this card.",printed,2006-07-21,7
  Ripple,keyword,702.60,Surging Dementia,"Written as ""Ripple X"", where X is a number When a spell is cast with Ripple, its controller may reveal the top X cards of their library and cast any copies of that card without paying the mana cost. This triggers ripple again.","When you cast this spell, you may reveal the top four cards of your library. You may cast spells with the same name as this spell from among those cards without paying their mana costs. Put the rest on the bottom of your library.",forge_oracle,2006-07-21,5
  Split Second,keyword,702.61,Angel's Grace,"A card with split second cannot be interacted with. Once it is on the stack, nothing else can be put there until it has resolved.","As long as this spell is on the stack, players can't cast spells or activate abilities that aren't mana abilities.",printed,2006-10-06,25
  Suspend,keyword,702.62,Rift Bolt,"Written as ""Suspend X [cost]"", where X is a number You may pay the suspend cost for a card and exile it with X time counters on it. At the beginning of your upkeep, remove a time counter from the card. When the last time counter is removed, you may then cast t","Rather than cast this card from your hand, you may pay {C}{C} and exile it with three time counters on it. At the beginning of your upkeep, remove a time counter. When the last is removed, you may cast it without paying its mana cost.",printed,2006-10-06,73
  Vanishing,keyword,702.63,702.63,"Vanishing is a keyword that represents three abilities. ""Vanishing N"" means ""This permanent enters with N time counters on it,"" ""At the beginning of your upkeep, if this permanent has a time counter on it, remove a time counter from it,"" and ""When the last time counter is removed from this permanent","This creature enters with three time counters on it. At the beginning of your upkeep, remove a time counter from it. When the last is removed, sacrifice it.",printed,,
  Absorb,keyword,702.64,,"Only on one card: Lymph Sliver Written as ""Absorb X"" where X is a number","Absorb is a static ability. ""Absorb N"" means ""If a source would deal damage to this creature, prevent N of that damage.""",cr_subrule_a,,
  Aura Swap,keyword,702.65,Arcanum Wings,"Written as ""Aura Swap X"", where X is a mana cost When a card with aura swap is attached to a creature, you may pay the cost associated with aura swap to return the attached card to your hand and attach an aura from your hand to the same creature.",{C}{C}: Exchange this Aura with an Aura card in your hand.,printed,2007-05-04,1
  Delve,keyword,702.66,Treasure Cruise,"Delve allows you to exile cards from your graveyard to pay the generic mana cost of the card with delve. For example, with Treasure Cruise if you have 12 cards in your graveyard, you may pay 1 blue mana and ""delve"" 7 cards to draw 3 cards while only paying 1 m",Each card you exile from your graveyard while casting this spell pays for {C}.,printed,2013-06-07,30
  Fortify,keyword,702.67,702.67,"Fortify is an activated ability of Fortification cards. ""Fortify [cost]"" means ""[Cost]: Attach this Fortification to target land you control. Activate only as a sorcery.""",{C}: Attach to target land you control. Fortify only as a sorcery.,printed,,
  Frenzy,keyword,702.68,Frenzy Sliver,"Written as ""Frenzy X"" where X is a number Whenever a creature with frenzy attacks and isn't blocked, it gets +X/+0 until the end of turn.","Whenever this creature attacks and isn't blocked, it gets +N/+N until end of turn.",scryfall_api,,
  Gravestorm,keyword,702.69,Bitter Ordeal,"When the spell is cast, copy it for each permanent that entered the graveyard this turn. Only on one card with the mechanic.","When you cast this spell, copy it for each permanent put into a graveyard from the battlefield this turn.",printed,2007-05-04,3
  Poisonous,keyword,702.70,Virulent Sliver,"Written as ""Poisonous X"", where X is a number Whenever a creature with poisonous deals damage to a player, that player gets X poison counters, where X is the number associated with the ability. If a player has 10 poison counters, they lose the game.","Poisonous is a triggered ability. ""Poisonous N"" means ""Whenever this creature deals combat damage to a player, that player gets N poison counters."" (For information about poison counters, see rule 104.3d.)",cr_rule_702.70a,,
  Transfigure,keyword,702.71,Fleshwrither,"Written as ""Transfigure [cost]"" Any time a sorcery could be cast, you may pay the transfigure cost and sacrifice the creature with transfigure to search your library for a creature with the same mana value.","{C}{C}{C}, Sacrifice this creature: Search your library for a creature card with the same mana value as this creature, put that card onto the battlefield, then shuffle. Transfigure only as a sorcery.",printed,2007-05-04,1
  Champion,keyword,702.72,Wanderwine Prophets,"Written as ""Champion a [creature type]"" When you cast a creature with champion, you must exile a card that is the type referred to in the champion keyword. If the champion card leaves play, the exiled card will be returned to the battlefield.","When this enters, sacrifice it unless you exile another creature you control. When this leaves the battlefield, that card returns to the battlefield.",printed,2007-10-12,12
  Changeling,keyword,702.73,Chameleon Colossus,"Creatures with changeling count as all creature types, therefore benefitting from all bonuses associated with tribal synergies. Very common in decks without many good creatures of a specific type.",This card is every creature type.,printed,2007-10-12,67
  Evoke,keyword,702.74,Mulldrifter,"You may cast a card for its evoke cost, but when it enters the battlefield, it is immediately sacrificed. The evoke cost is usually much less than the cost of casting the card.","You may cast this spell for its evoke cost. If you do, it's sacrificed when it enters.",printed,2007-10-12,37
  Hideaway,keyword,702.75,Mosswort Bridge,"When a card with hideaway enters the battlefield, you look at the top 4 cards of your library. Exile one card under the hideaway permanent. Then, when a condition is met, you cast the exiled card without paying its mana cost. Only on 5 cards from a set called","When this permanent enters, look at the top four cards of your library, exile one face down, then put the rest on the bottom of your library.",printed,2007-10-12,15
  Prowl,keyword,702.76,Latchkey Faerie,"Written as ""Prowl [cost]"" A creature may be cast for its prowl cost, only if a creature that shares a creature type dealt damage to a player this turn.",You may cast this for its prowl cost if you dealt combat damage to a player this turn with a Rogue.,forge_oracle,2008-02-01,10
  Reinforce,keyword,702.77,Burrenton Bombardier,"Written as ""Reinforce: X - [cost]"", where X is a number You may discard a card with reinforce from your hand and pay the reinforce cost, then put X +1/+1 counters on target creature","{C}{C}, Discard this card: Put a +N/+N counter on target creature.",printed,2008-02-01,11
  Conspire,keyword,702.78,Giantbaiting,"Only on instants and sorceries. When you cast a spell with conspire, you may tap 2 creatures that share a color with the spell. If you do, copy that spell.","As you cast this spell, you may tap two untapped creatures you control that share a color with it. When you do, copy it and you may choose a new target for the copy.",printed,2008-05-02,11
  Persist,keyword,702.79,Kitchen Finks,"If a creature with persist is put into a graveyard from play and had no -1/-1 counters on it, return it to the battlefield with a -1/-1 counter. Doubles up enter the battlefield triggers and death triggers and stuff.","When this creature dies, if it had no -N/-N counters on it, return it to the battlefield under its owner's control with a -N/-N counter on it.",printed,2008-05-02,25
  Wither,keyword,702.80,Harvest Gwyllion,"Wither is a replacement effect. If a creature would be dealt nonlethal damage by a creature with wither, it instead has -1/-1 counters placed on it instead of marking normal damage. This is similar to infect, but players do not receive poison counters from cre",This deals damage to creatures in the form of -N/-N counters.,printed,2008-05-02,27
  Retrace,keyword,702.81,Oona's Grace,"Cards with retrace may be cast from the graveyard if you discard a land card in addition to paying their other costs. Unlike most other versions of this, they are not exiled once cast from the graveyard, so you can keep retracing them as long as you have lands",You may cast this card from your graveyard by discarding a land card in addition to paying its other costs.,printed,2008-07-25,18
  Devour,keyword,702.82,Predator Dragon,"Written as ""Devour X"", where X is a number Whenever a creature with devour enters the battlefield, you may sacrifice any number of creatures you control. The creature with devour then gets X +1/+1 counters for each creature sacrificed this way.","As this enters, you may sacrifice any number of creatures. This creature enters with that many +N/+N counters on it.",printed,2008-10-03,23
  Exalted,keyword,702.83,Noble Hierarch,"Whenever a creature you control attacks alone, it gets +1/+1 for each instance of exalted. If you have 2 creatures with exalted, and one of them attacks alone, that is 2 instances of exalted, so that creatures ends up getting +2/+2.","Whenever a creature you control attacks alone, that creature gets +N/+N until end of turn.",printed,2008-10-03,36
  Unearth,keyword,702.84,Dregscape Zombie,"Written as ""Unearth [cost]"" When a creature with unearth is in the graveyard, you may pay the unearth cost any time you could play a sorcery. Return that creature to the battlefield, and it gains haste. Exile it at the end step.",{C}{C}: Return this card from your graveyard to the battlefield. It gains haste. Exile it at the beginning of the next end step or if it would leave the battlefield. Unearth only as a sorcery.,printed,2008-10-03,58
  Cascade,keyword,702.85,Bloodbraid Elf,"Whenever a you cast a card with cascade, exile the top card of your library until you find a card with a lesser converted mana cost, then you may cast that card without paying its mana cost. 2 spells for the cost of 1 spell. Very powerful, considered broken.","When you cast this spell, exile cards from the top of your library until you exile a nonland card that costs less. You may cast it without paying its mana cost. Put the exiled cards on the bottom in a random order.",printed,2009-04-30,37
  Annihilator,keyword,702.86,Ulamog's Crusher,"Written as ""Annihilator X"", where X is a number Whenever a creature with annihilator attacks, the defending player sacrifices X permanents, where X is the number associated with annihilator.","Whenever this creature attacks, defending player sacrifices two permanents.",printed,2010-04-23,14
  Level Up,keyword,702.87,Lighthouse Chronologist,"Cards with level up enter the battlefield at level 0. You may pay the level up cost to put a level counter on that creature. As creatures ""gain experience (level up)"", they gain more abilities. You may only level up as a sorcery, but may do so as many times as",{C}: Put a level counter on this. Level up only as a sorcery.,printed,2010-04-23,26
  Rebound,keyword,702.88,Ephemerate,"Whenever you cast a card with rebound, exile it. You may cast that card again without paying its mana cost on your next upkeep.","If you cast this spell from your hand, exile it as it resolves. At the beginning of your next upkeep, you may cast this card from exile without paying its mana cost.",printed,2010-04-23,36
  Umbra Armor,keyword,702.89,702.89,"Umbra armor is a static ability that appears on some Auras. ""Umbra armor"" means ""If enchanted permanent would be destroyed, instead remove all damage marked on it and destroy this Aura.""","If enchanted creature would be destroyed, instead remove all damage from it and destroy this Aura.",printed,,
  Infect,keyword,702.90,Phyrexian Juggernaut,Damage it deals to creatures is dealt as -1/-1 counters and damage to players gives poison counters instead of life loss. A player with 10 poison counters loses.,This creature deals damage to creatures in the form of -N/-N counters and to players in the form of poison counters.,printed,,
  Battle Cry,keyword,702.91,Signal Pest,"Whenever a creature with battle cry attacks, other attacking creatures get +1/+0 until the end of turn.","Whenever this creature attacks, each other attacking creature gets +N/+N until end of turn.",printed,2011-02-04,14
  Living Weapon,keyword,702.92,Batterskull,"Cards with living weapon are equipment. When they enter the battlefield, they generate a 0/0 black germ creature token, and attach themselves to that creature. Since the germs have no abilities and are 0/0 creatures, they will die if the equipment becomes unat","When this Equipment enters, create a N/N black Phyrexian Germ creature token, then attach this to it.",printed,2011-02-04,19
  Undying,keyword,702.93,Young Wolf,"When a creature with undying is put into the graveyard, if it had no +1/+1 counters, return it to the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter. Yes, this is persist with +1 counters instead of -1 counters.","When this creature dies, if it had no +N/+N counters on it, return it to the battlefield under its owner's control with a +N/+N counter on it.",printed,2012-02-03,23
  Miracle,keyword,702.94,Temporal Mastery,"You may cast a card for its miracle cost if it is the first card you draw in a turn. Since the timing on miracles is different, if you draw a sorcery on an opponent's turn and it has miracle, you may cast it for its miracle cost, even though it is a sorcery.",You may cast this card for its miracle cost when you draw it if it's the first card you drew this turn.,printed,2012-05-04,19
  Soulbond,keyword,702.95,Deadeye Navigator,Creatures with souldbond enter the battlefield and bond to another creature. Both creatures then gain some boon.,You may pair this creature with another unpaired creature when either enters. They remain paired for as long as you control both of them.,printed,2012-05-04,26
  Overload,keyword,702.96,Vandalblast,"Written as ""Overload [cost]"" When an instant or sorcery is overloaded, instead of targeting 1 target, it affects all targets.","You may cast this spell for its overload cost. If you do, change ""target"" in its text to ""each.""",printed,2012-10-05,28
  Scavenge,keyword,702.97,Deadbridge Goliath,"Written as ""Scavenge [cost]"" You may exile a card with scavenge from your graveyard by paying it's scavenge cost. Then, place a number of +1/+1 counters on target creature.","{C}{C}{C}, Exile this card from your graveyard: Put a number of +N/+N counters equal to this card's power on target creature. Scavenge only as a sorcery.",printed,2012-10-05,14
  Unleash,keyword,702.98,Rakdos Cackler,"When a creature with unleash enters the battlefield, its controller may choose to have it enter with a +1/+1 counter on it. If a creature with unleash has a counter on it, it cannot block. The counter does not have to come from unleash, it's any +1/+1 counter.",You may have this creature enter with a +N/+N counter on it. It can't block as long as it has a +N/+N counter on it.,printed,2012-10-05,14
  Cipher,keyword,702.99,Call of the Nightwing,"When you cast a spell with cipher, you may exile it as it resolves. Then, choose a creature to ""cipher"" the spell onto. Whenever that creature deals damage to an opponent, you may cast the ""ciphered"" spell without paying its cost. Sounds really strong, but usu","Then you may exile this spell card encoded on a creature you control. Whenever that creature deals combat damage to a player, its controller may cast a copy of the encoded card without paying its mana cost.",printed,2013-02-01,15
  Evolve,keyword,702.100,Experiment One,"Whenever a creature with power or toughness greater than a creature with evolve enters the battlefield, put a +1/+1 counter on the creature with evolve. If you play Experiment One on turn 1, then Watchwolf on turn 2, Experiment One will have a +1/+1 counter pu","Whenever a creature you control enters, if that creature has greater power or toughness than this creature, put a +N/+N counter on this creature.",printed,2013-02-01,23
  Extort,keyword,702.101,Blind Obedience,"Whenever you cast a spell you may pay either white or black mana. If you do, each opponent loses 1 life and you gain life equal to the amount of life lost this way. Because the white mana symbol on extort cards is in the reminder text, extort cards can be play","Whenever you cast a spell, you may pay {C}. If you do, each opponent loses N life and you gain that much life.",printed,2013-02-01,18
  Fuse,keyword,702.102,702.102,"Fuse is a static ability found on some split cards (see rule 709, ""Split Cards"") that applies while the card with fuse is in a player's hand. If a player casts a split card with fuse from their hand, the player may choose to cast both halves of that split card rather than choose one half. This choic",You may cast one or both halves of this card from your hand.,printed,,
  Bestow,keyword,702.103,Celestial Archon,"Written as ""Bestow [cost]"" When you pay the bestow cost, you use a creature with bestow as an aura for a creature on the battlefield. If the bestowed creature dies, the creature with bestow stays on the battlefield.","If you cast this card for its bestow cost, it's an Aura spell with enchant creature. It becomes a creature again if it's not attached.",printed,2013-09-27,43
  Tribute,keyword,702.104,Fanatic of Xenagos,"Written as ""Tribute X"", where X is a number. Whenever a creature with tribute enters the battlefield, an opponent may pay ""tribute"" by putting X +1/+1 counters on it. If the tribute is not paid, some other effect will occur.","As this creature enters, an opponent of your choice may put two +N/+N counters on it.",printed,2014-02-07,11
  Dethrone,keyword,702.105,702.105,"Dethrone is a triggered ability. ""Dethrone"" means ""Whenever this creature attacks the player with the most life or tied for most life, put a +1/+1 counter on this creature.""","Whenever this creature attacks the player with the most life or tied for most life, put a +N/+N counter on it.",printed,,
  Hidden Agenda,keyword,702.106,702.106,"Hidden agenda is a static ability that functions as a conspiracy card with hidden agenda is put into the command zone. ""Hidden agenda"" means ""As you put this conspiracy card into the command zone, turn it face down and secretly choose a card name.""",Start the game with this conspiracy face down in the command zone and secretly choose a card name. You may turn this conspiracy face up any time and reveal that name.,printed,,
  Outlast,keyword,702.107,702.107,"Outlast is an activated ability. ""Outlast [cost]"" means ""[Cost], {T}: Put a +1/+1 counter on this creature. Activate only as a sorcery.""","{C}, {C}: Put a +N/+N counter on this creature. Outlast only as a sorcery.",printed,,
  Prowess,keyword,702.108,Monastery Swiftspear,"Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, prowess creatures get +1/+1 until end of turn. Does stack, so if you cast 2 noncreature spells, prowess creatures get +1/+1 for each of those spells, getting +2/+2 total.","Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, this creature gets +N/+N until end of turn.",printed,2014-09-26,102
  Dash,keyword,702.109,"Ragavan, Nimble Pilferer","You may pay the dash cost for a creature, that creature gains haste and returns to your hand at the end of the turn. Helps you dodge sorcery speed removal spells, like board sweepers.","You may cast this spell for its dash cost. If you do, it gains haste, and it's returned from the battlefield to its owner's hand at the beginning of the next end step.",printed,2015-01-23,22
  Exploit,keyword,702.110,Fell Stinger,"Whenever you cast a card with exploit, as an additional cost, you may sacrifice a creature. If you do, you gain some benefit.","When this creature enters, you may sacrifice a creature.",printed,2015-03-27,23
  Menace,keyword,702.111,Ruin Grinder,"Creatures with menace can only be blocked by 2 or more creatures. When paired with deathtouch, it's very potent.",This creature can't be blocked except by two or more creatures.,printed,2004-10-01,419
  Renown,keyword,702.112,Scab-Clan Berserker,"Written as ""Reinforce X"", where X is a number. Whenever a creature with renown deals combat damage to a player for the first time, put X +1/+1 counters on it. It then becomes renown.","When this creature deals combat damage to a player, if it isn't renowned, put a +N/+N counter on it and it becomes renowned.",printed,2015-07-17,20
  Awaken,keyword,702.113,702.113,"Awaken appears on some instants and sorceries. It represents two abilities: a static ability that functions while the spell with awaken is on the stack and a spell ability. ""Awaken N— [cost]"" means ""You may pay [cost] rather than pay this spell's mana cost as you cast this spell"" and ""If this spell'","If you cast this spell for {C}{C}, also put four +N/+N counters on target land you control and it becomes a N/N Elemental creature with haste. It's still a land.",printed,,
  Devoid,keyword,702.114,Void Grafter,The card is colorless even though its mana cost has colored symbols.,This card has no color.,forge_oracle,,
  Ingest,keyword,702.115,702.115,"Ingest is a triggered ability. ""Ingest"" means ""Whenever this creature deals combat damage to a player, that player exiles the top card of their library.""","Whenever this creature deals combat damage to a player, that player exiles the top card of their library.",printed,,
  Myriad,keyword,702.116,702.116,"Myriad is a triggered ability that may also create a delayed triggered ability. ""Myriad"" means ""Whenever this creature attacks, for each opponent other than defending player, you may create a token that's a copy of this creature that's tapped and attacking that player or a planeswalker they control.","Whenever this creature attacks, for each opponent other than defending player, you may create a token copy that's tapped and attacking that player or a planeswalker they control. Exile the tokens at end of combat.",printed,,
  Surge,keyword,702.117,702.117,"Surge is a static ability that functions while the spell with surge is on the stack. ""Surge [cost]"" means ""You may pay [cost] rather than pay this spell's mana cost as you cast this spell if you or one of your teammates has cast another spell this turn."" Casting a spell for its surge cost follows th",You may cast this spell for its surge cost if you or a teammate has cast another spell this turn.,printed,,
  Skulk,keyword,702.118,702.118,Skulk is an evasion ability.,This creature can't be blocked by creatures with greater power.,printed,,
  Emerge,keyword,702.119,,Emerge allows you to sacrifice a creature and pay the difference between the sacrificed creature's mana cost and the emerge cost. Very similar to offering mechanic in that way.,You may cast this spell by sacrificing a creature and paying the emerge cost reduced by that creature's mana value.,printed,2016-07-22,15
  Escalate,keyword,702.120,702.120,"Escalate is a static ability of modal spells (see rule 700.2) that functions while the spell with escalate is on the stack. ""Escalate [cost]"" means ""For each mode you choose beyond the first as you cast this spell, you pay an additional [cost]."" Paying a spell's escalate cost follows the rules for p",Pay this cost for each mode chosen beyond the first.,printed,,
  Melee,keyword,702.121,702.121,"Melee is a triggered ability. ""Melee"" means ""Whenever this creature attacks, it gets +1/+1 until end of turn for each opponent you attacked with a creature this combat.""","Whenever this creature attacks, it gets +N/+N until end of turn for each opponent you attacked this combat.",printed,,
  Crew,keyword,702.122,Aethersphere Harvester,"Written as ""Crew X"" where X is a number Only on vehicles. To crew a vehicle, you must tap any number of creatures whos power equals X or greater.",Tap any number of creatures you control with total power N or more: This Vehicle becomes an artifact creature until end of turn.,printed,2016-09-30,196
  Fabricate,keyword,702.123,702.123,"Fabricate is a triggered ability. ""Fabricate N"" means ""When this permanent enters, you may put N +1/+1 counters on it. If you don't, create N 1/1 colorless Servo artifact creature tokens.""","When this creature enters, put a +N/+N counter on it or create a N/N colorless Servo artifact creature token.",printed,,
  Partner,keyword,702.124,Lore Weaver,Commander rule keyword. Two commanders that both have partner can be the same deck's commanders. Variants (Partner with,You can have two commanders if both have partner.,printed,,
  Undaunted,keyword,702.125,702.125,"Undaunted is a static ability that functions while the spell with undaunted is on the stack. Undaunted means ""This spell costs {1} less to cast for each opponent you have.""",This spell costs {C} less to cast for each opponent.,printed,,
  Improvise,keyword,702.126,702.126,"Improvise is a static ability that functions while the spell with improvise is on the stack. ""Improvise"" means ""For each generic mana in this spell's total cost, you may tap an untapped artifact you control rather than pay that mana.""",Your artifacts can help cast this spell. Each artifact you tap after you're done activating mana abilities pays for {C}.,printed,,
  Aftermath,keyword,702.127,Commit to Memory,"Only on split cards One side may only be cast from your hand, the other side may only be cast from the graveyard.",Cast this spell only from your graveyard. Then exile it.,scryfall_api,2017-04-28,27
  Embalm,keyword,702.128,Aven Wind Guide,"Written as ""Embalm [cost]"" When a creature is in the graveyard, you may pay the embalm cost to exile that creature from your graveyard and make a token of it.","{C}{C}, Exile this card from your graveyard: Create a token that's a copy of it, except it's a white Zombie Human Warrior with no mana cost. Embalm only as a sorcery.",printed,2017-04-28,15
  Eternalize,keyword,702.129,702.129,"Eternalize is an activated ability that functions while the card with eternalize is in a graveyard. ""Eternalize [cost]"" means ""[Cost], Exile this card from your graveyard: Create a token that's a copy of this card, except it's black, it's 4/4, it has no mana cost, and it's a Zombie in addition to it","{C}{C}{C}, Exile this card from your graveyard: Create a token that's a copy of it, except it's a N/N black Zombie Human Shaman with no mana cost. Eternalize only as a sorcery.",printed,,
  Afflict,keyword,702.130,702.130,"Afflict is a triggered ability. ""Afflict N"" means ""Whenever this creature becomes blocked, defending player loses N life.""","Whenever this creature becomes blocked, defending player loses N life.",printed,,
  Ascend,keyword,702.131,702.131,"Ascend on an instant or sorcery spell represents a spell ability. It means ""If you control ten or more permanents and you don't have the city's blessing, you get the city's blessing for the rest of the game.""","If you control ten or more permanents, you get the city's blessing for the rest of the game.",printed,,
  Assist,keyword,702.132,702.132,"Assist is a static ability that modifies the rules of paying for the spell with assist (see rules 601.2g-h). If the total cost to cast a spell with assist includes a generic mana component, before you activate mana abilities while casting it, you may choose another player. That player has a chance t",Another player can pay up to {C} of this spell's cost.,printed,,
  Jump-Start,keyword,702.133,Radical Idea,Cards with Jump-start may be cast from the graveyard by paying their mana cost and discarding a card.,You may cast this card from your graveyard by discarding a card in addition to paying its other costs. Then exile this card.,printed,2018-10-05,13
  Mentor,keyword,702.134,Legion Warboss,"Whenever a card with mentor attacks, put a +1/+1 counter on target attacking creature with less power than the mentor creature. If for some reason, a mentor card is put into the battlefield attacking, it does not trigger mentor. The act of declaring it as an a","Whenever this creature attacks, put a +N/+N counter on target attacking creature with lesser power.",printed,2018-10-05,21
  Afterlife,keyword,702.135,Orzhov Enforcer,"Written as ""Afterlife X"", where X is an number When a creature with afterlife dies, it's controller creates X 1/1 black and white spirit tokens with flying equal to the afterlife number.","When this creature dies, create a N/N white and black Spirit creature token with flying.",printed,2019-01-25,11
  Riot,keyword,702.136,Gruul Spellbreaker,"Whenever a creature with riot enters the battlefield, its controller chooses for it to enter with either a +1/+1 counter and haste.",This creature enters with your choice of a +N/+N counter or haste.,printed,2019-01-25,13
  Spectacle,keyword,702.137,Light up the Stage,"Written as ""Spectacle [cost]"" You may cast a card for its spectacle cost if an opponent was dealt damage this turn.",You may cast this spell for its spectacle cost rather than its mana cost if an opponent lost life this turn.,printed,2019-01-25,11
  Escape,keyword,702.138,Cling to Dust,"Written as ""Escape [cost]"" You may cast a card from the graveyard for it's escape cost by exiling a specified amount of other cards from your graveyard.","Escape represents a static ability that functions while the card with escape is in a player's graveyard. ""Escape [cost]"" means ""You may cast this card from your graveyard by paying [cost] rather than paying its mana cost."" Casting a spell using its escape ability follows the rules for paying alternative costs in rules 601.2b and 601.2f–h.",cr_rule_702.138a,2020-01-24,33
  Companion,keyword,702.139,702.139,"Companion is a keyword ability that functions outside the game. It's written as ""Companion—[Condition]."" Before the game begins, you may reveal one card you own from outside the game with a companion ability whose condition is fulfilled by your starting deck. (See rule 103.2b.) Once during the game,","Companion is a keyword ability that functions outside the game. It's written as ""Companion-[Condition]."" Before the game begins, you may reveal one card you own from outside the game with a companion ability whose condition is fulfilled by your starting deck. (See rule 103.2b.) Once during the game, any time you have priority and the stack is empty, but only during a main phase of your turn, you may pay {3} and put t",cr_rule_702.139a,,
  Mutate,keyword,702.140,Dirge Bat,"Written as ""Mutate [cost]"" Creatures may be cast for their mutate cost if targeting a non-human creature you control to mutate onto.","If you cast this spell for its mutate cost, put it over or under target non-Human creature you own. They mutate into the creature on top plus all abilities from under it.",printed,2020-04-17,34
  Encore,keyword,702.141,702.141,"Encore is an activated ability that functions while the card with encore is in a graveyard. ""Encore [cost]"" means ""[Cost], Exile this card from your graveyard: For each opponent, create a token that's a copy of this card that attacks that opponent this turn if able. The tokens gain haste. Sacrifice","{C}{C}{C}, Exile this card from your graveyard: For each opponent, create a token copy that attacks that opponent this turn if able. They gain haste. Sacrifice them at the beginning of the next end step. Activate only as a sorcery.",printed,,
  Boast,keyword,702.142,702.142,"Boast is a keyword that adds additional rules to the activated ability that follows it. ""Boast — [Cost]: [Effect]"" means ""[Cost]: [Effect]. Activate only if this creature attacked this turn and only once each turn.""",Activate only if this creature attacked this turn and only once each turn.,scryfall_api,,
  Foretell,keyword,702.143,Doomskar,"Written as ""Foretell [cost]"" During your turn, at any time, you may pay 2 to ""foretell"" a card. You may cast that card for its foretell cost on a later turn.","During your turn, you may pay {C} and exile this card from your hand face down. Cast it on a later turn for its foretell cost.",printed,2021-02-05,52
  Demonstrate,keyword,702.144,702.144,"Demonstrate is a triggered ability. ""Demonstrate"" means ""When you cast this spell, you may copy it and you may choose new targets for the copy. If you copy the spell, choose an opponent. That player copies the spell and may choose new targets for that copy.""","When you cast this spell, you may copy it. If you do, choose an opponent to also copy it. Players may choose new targets for their copies.",printed,,
  Daybound and Nightbound,keyword,702.145,Bird Admirer,,"If a player casts no spells during their own turn, it becomes night next turn.",printed,,
  Disturb,keyword,702.146,Lunarch Veteran,"Written as ""Disturb [cost]"" Whenever a card with disturb is in your graveyard, you may cast it for its disturb cost. When you do, it enters the battlefield transformed.",You may cast this card from your graveyard transformed for its disturb cost.,printed,2021-09-24,25
  Decayed,keyword,702.147,702.147,"Decayed represents a static ability and a triggered ability. ""Decayed"" means ""This creature can't block"" and ""When this creature attacks, sacrifice it at end of combat.""","This creature can't block. When it attacks, sacrifice it at end of combat.",printed,,
  Cleave,keyword,702.148,702.148,"Cleave is a keyword that represents two static abilities that function while a spell with cleave is on the stack. ""Cleave [cost]"" means ""You may cast this spell by paying [cost] rather than paying its mana cost"" and ""If this spell's cleave cost was paid, change its text by removing all text found wi","You may cast this spell for its cleave cost. If you do, remove the words in square brackets.",printed,,
  Training,keyword,702.149,702.149,"Training is a triggered ability. ""Training"" means ""Whenever this creature and at least one other creature with power greater than this creature's power attack, put a +1/+1 counter on this creature.""","Whenever this creature attacks with another creature with greater power, put a +N/+N counter on this creature.",printed,,
  Compleated,keyword,702.150,702.150,"Compleated is a static ability found on some planeswalker cards. Compleated means ""If this permanent would enter with one or more loyalty counters on it and the player who cast it chose to pay life for any part of its cost represented by Phyrexian mana symbols, it instead enters the battlefield with","{C} can be paid with {C}, {C}, or N life. If life was paid, this planeswalker enters with two fewer loyalty counters.",printed,,
  Reconfigure,action,702.151,The Reality Chip,"Written as ""Reconfigure X"" where X is a mana cost These are artifact creatures that are also equipment.","{C}: Attach to target creature you control; or unattach from a creature. Reconfigure only as a sorcery. While attached, this isn't a creature.",printed,2022-02-18,21
  Blitz,keyword,702.152,,"Written as ""Blitz [cost]"" You may cast a card for it's blitz cost. If you do, it gains haste. Sacrifice it at the next end step and draw a card.","If you cast this spell for its blitz cost, it gains haste and ""When this creature dies, draw a card."" Sacrifice it at the beginning of the next end step.",printed,2022-04-29,19
  Casualty,keyword,702.153,A Little Chat,"Written as ""Casualty X"", where X is a number When you cast a card with casualty, you may sacrifice a creature with power equal to the X value. If you do, copy the spell.","As you cast this spell, you may sacrifice a creature with power N or greater. When you do, copy this spell and you may choose new targets for the copy.",printed,2022-04-29,16
  Enlist,keyword,702.154,702.154,"Enlist represents a static ability and a triggered ability. Enlist means ""As this creature attacks, you may tap up to one untapped creature you control that you didn't choose to attack with and that either has haste or has been under your control continuously since this turn began. When you do, this","As this creature attacks, you may tap a nonattacking creature you control without summoning sickness. When you do, add its power to this creature's until end of turn.",printed,,
  Read Ahead,keyword,702.155,702.155,"Read ahead is a keyword found on some Saga cards. ""Read ahead"" means ""Chapter abilities of this Saga can't trigger the turn it entered the battlefield unless it has exactly the number of lore counters on it specified in the chapter symbol of that ability."" See rule 714, ""Saga Cards.""",Choose a chapter and start with that many lore counters. Add one after your draw step. Skipped chapters don't trigger. Sacrifice after III.,printed,,
  Ravenous,keyword,702.156,702.156,"Ravenous is a keyword found on some creature cards with {X} in their mana cost. Ravenous represents both a replacement effect and a triggered ability. ""Ravenous"" means ""This permanent enters with X +1/+1 counters on it"" and ""When this permanent enters, if X is 5 or more, draw a card."" See rule 107.3","This creature enters with X +N/+N counters on it. If X is N or more, draw a card when it enters.",printed,,
  Squad,keyword,702.157,702.157,"Squad is a keyword that represents two linked abilities. The first is a static ability that functions while the creature spell with squad is on the stack. The second is a triggered ability that functions when the creature with squad enters the battlefield. ""Squad [cost]"" means ""As an additional cost","As an additional cost to cast this spell, you may pay {C} any number of times. When this creature enters, create that many tokens that are copies of it.",printed,,
  Space Sculptor,keyword,702.158,702.158,One card (Space Beleren) has the space sculptor ability. This keyword ability causes creatures to gain sector designations.,"Space Beleren divides the battlefield into alpha, beta, and gamma sectors. If a creature isn't assigned to a sector, its controller assigns it to one. Opponents assign first.",printed,,
  Visit,keyword,702.159,702.159,"Visit is a keyword ability found on Attraction cards (see rule 717). ""Visit — [Effect]"" means ""Whenever you roll to visit your Attractions, if the result is equal to a number that is lit up on this Attraction, [effect]."" See rule 701.52, ""Roll to Visit Your Attractions.""","Visit is a keyword ability found on Attraction cards (see rule 717). ""Visit - [Effect]"" means ""Whenever you roll to visit your Attractions, if the result is equal to a number that is lit up on this Attraction, [effect]."" See rule 701.52, ""Roll to Visit Your Attractions.""",cr_rule_702.159a,,
  Prototype,keyword,702.160,702.160,"Prototype is a static ability that appears on prototype cards that have a secondary set of power, toughness, and mana cost characteristics. A player who casts a spell with prototype can choose to cast that card ""prototyped."" If they do, the alternative set of its power, toughness, and mana cost char","You may cast this spell with different mana cost, color, and size. It keeps its abilities and types.",printed,,
  Living Metal,keyword,702.161,702.161,"Living metal is a keyword ability found on some Vehicles. ""Living metal"" means ""During your turn, this permanent is an artifact creature in addition to its other types.""","Living metal is a keyword ability found on some Vehicles. ""Living metal"" means ""During your turn, this permanent is an artifact creature in addition to its other types.""",cr_rule_702.161a,,
  More Than Meets the Eye,keyword,702.162,702.162,"More Than Meets the Eye represents a static ability that functions in any zone from which the spell may be cast. ""More Than Meets the Eye [cost]"" means ""You may cast this card converted by paying [cost] rather than its mana cost."" Casting a spell using its More Than Meets the Eye ability follows the",You may cast this card converted for {C}{C}.,printed,,
  For Mirrodin!,keyword,702.163,702.163,"For Mirrodin! is a triggered ability. ""For Mirrodin!"" means ""When this Equipment enters, create a 2/2 red Rebel creature token, then attach this Equipment to it.""","When this Equipment enters, create a N/N red Rebel creature token, then attach this to it.",printed,,
  Toxic,keyword,702.164,Tyrranax Atrocity,Written as Toxic X. When the creature deals combat damage to a player that player also gets X poison counters in addition to the normal damage.,Players dealt combat damage by this creature also get a poison counter.,printed,,
  Backup,keyword,702.165,702.165,"Backup is a triggered ability. ""Backup N"" means ""When this creature enters, put N +1/+1 counters on target creature. If that's another creature, it also gains the non-backup abilities of this creature printed below this one until end of turn."" Cards with backup have one or more abilities printed aft","When this creature enters, put a +N/+N counter on target creature. If that's another creature, it gains the following ability until end of turn.",printed,,
  Bargain,keyword,702.166,702.166,"Bargain is a static ability that functions while the spell with bargain is on the stack. ""Bargain"" means ""As an additional cost to cast this spell, you may sacrifice an artifact, enchantment, or token."" Paying a spell's bargain cost follows the rules for paying additional costs in rules 601.2b and 6","You may sacrifice an artifact, enchantment, or token as you cast this spell.",printed,,
  Craft,keyword,702.167,702.167,"Craft represents an activated ability. It is written as ""Craft with [materials] [cost],"" where [materials] is a description of one or more objects. It means ""[Cost], Exile this permanent, Exile [materials] from among permanents you control and/or cards in your graveyard: Return this card to the batt","{C}{C}{C}, Exile this artifact, Exile another artifact you control or an artifact card from your graveyard: Return this card transformed under its owner's control. Craft only as a sorcery.",printed,,
  Disguise,keyword,702.168,702.168,"Disguise is a static ability that functions in any zone from which you could play the card it's on, and the disguise effect works any time the card is face down. ""Disguise [cost]"" means ""You may cast this card as a 2/2 face-down creature with ward {2}, no name, no subtypes, and no mana cost by payin",You may cast this card face down for {C} as a N/N creature with ward {C}. Turn it face up any time for its disguise cost.,printed,,
  Solved,keyword,702.169,702.169,"Solved is a keyword ability found on Case cards. See rule 719, ""Case Cards."" ""Solved"" is followed by ability text. Together, they represent a static ability, a triggered ability, or an activated ability.","Solved is a keyword ability found on Case cards. See rule 719, ""Case Cards."" ""Solved"" is followed by ability text. Together, they represent a static ability, a triggered ability, or an activated ability.",cr_rule_702.169a,,
  Plot,keyword,702.170,Unscrupulous Contractor,Written as Plot [cost]. Pay the plot cost at sorcery timing to exile the card; on a later turn cast it from exile for free at sorcery timing.,You may pay {C}{C} and exile this card from your hand. Cast it as a sorcery on a later turn without paying its mana cost. Plot only as a sorcery.,printed,,
  Saddle,keyword,702.171,Caustic Bronco,Written as Saddle X on Mounts. At sorcery timing tap other creatures with total power X or more; the Mount becomes saddled until end of turn and may use its saddled abilities.,Tap any number of other creatures you control with total power N or more: This Mount becomes saddled until end of turn. Saddle only as a sorcery.,printed,,
  Spree,keyword,702.172,702.172,"Spree is a static ability found on some modal spells (see rule 700.2) that applies while the spell on the stack. Spree means ""Choose one or more modes. As an additional cost to cast this spell, pay the costs associated with those modes.""",Choose one or more additional costs.,printed,,
  Freerunning,keyword,702.173,702.173,"Freerunning is a static ability that functions on the stack. ""Freerunning [cost]"" means ""You may pay [cost] rather than pay this spell's mana cost if a player was dealt combat damage this turn by a creature that, at the time it dealt that damage, was an Assassin creature or a commander under your co",You may cast this spell for its freerunning cost if you dealt combat damage to a player this turn with an Assassin or commander.,printed,,
  Gift,keyword,702.174,702.174,"Gift is a keyword that represents two abilities. It is written ""Gift a [something]."" The first ability is a static ability that functions while the card with gift is on the stack, and the second is either an ability that functions while the card with gift is on the stack or a triggered ability that","You may promise an opponent a gift as you cast this spell. If you do, they draw a card before its other effects.",printed,,
  Offspring,keyword,702.175,702.175,"Offspring represents two abilities. ""Offspring [cost]"" means ""You may pay an additional [cost] as you cast this spell"" and ""When this permanent enters, if its offspring cost was paid, create a token that's a copy of it, except it's 1/1.""","You may pay an additional {C} as you cast this spell. If you do, when this creature enters, create a N/N token copy of it.",printed,,
  Impending,keyword,702.176,702.176,Impending is a keyword that represents four abilities. The first is a static ability that functions while the spell with impending is on the stack. The second is static ability that creates a replacement effect that may apply to the permanent with impending as it enters the battlefield from the stac,"If you cast this spell for its impending cost, it enters with four time counters and isn't a creature until the last is removed. At the beginning of your end step, remove a time counter from it.",printed,,
  Exhaust,keyword,702.177,702.177,"Exhaust is a keyword that adds additional rules to the activated ability that follows it. ""Exhaust — [Cost]: [Effect]"" means ""[Cost]: [Effect]. Activate only once.""","Exhaust is a keyword that adds additional rules to the activated ability that follows it. ""Exhaust - [Cost]: [Effect]"" means ""[Cost]: [Effect]. Activate only once.""",cr_rule_702.177a,,
  Max Speed,keyword,702.178,702.178,"A max speed ability is a static ability. ""Max speed — [Ability]"" means ""As long as your speed is 4, this object has ‘[Ability].'"" See rule 702.179, ""Start Your Engines!"" 702.178b If an ability granted by a max speed ability states which zones it functions from, the max speed ability that grants that","A max speed ability is a static ability. ""Max speed - [Ability]"" means ""As long as your speed is 4, this object has ‘[Ability].'"" See rule 702.179, ""Start Your Engines!""",cr_rule_702.178a,,
  Start Your Engines!,keyword,702.179,702.179,"Start your engines! is a static ability. If a player controls a permanent with start your engines! and that player has no speed, their speed becomes 1. This is a state-based action. See rule 704.","If you have no speed, it starts at N. It increases once on each of your turns when an opponent loses life. Max speed is N.",printed,,
  Harmonize,keyword,702.180,702.180,"Harmonize represents three static abilities: one that functions while the card is in a player's graveyard and two that function while the spell with harmonize is on the stack. ""Harmonize [cost]"" means ""You may cast this card from your graveyard by paying [cost] and tapping up to one untapped creatur","You may cast this card from your graveyard for its harmonize cost. You may tap a creature you control to reduce that cost by {C}, where X is its power. Then exile this spell.",printed,,
  Mobilize,keyword,702.181,702.181,"Mobilize is a triggered ability. ""Mobilize N"" means ""Whenever this creature attacks, create N 1/1 red Warrior creature tokens. Those tokens enter tapped and attacking. Sacrifice them at the beginning of the next end step.""","Whenever this creature attacks, create a tapped and attacking N/N red Warrior creature token. Sacrifice it at the beginning of the next end step.",printed,,
  Job Select,keyword,702.182,702.182,"Job select is a triggered ability. ""Job select"" means ""When this Equipment enters, create a 1/1 colorless Hero creature token, then attach this Equipment to it.""","When this Equipment enters, create a N/N colorless Hero creature token, then attach this to it.",printed,,
  Tiered,keyword,702.183,702.183,"Tiered is a static ability found on some modal spells (see rule 700.2) that applies while the spell is on the stack. Tiered means ""Choose one. As an additional cost to cast this spell, pay the cost associated with that mode."" 702.184. Station",Choose one additional cost.,printed,,
  Station,keyword,702.184,Wedgelight Rammer,Written as Station on Spacecraft. Tap another creature you control to put charge counters equal to its power on the Spacecraft; at certain counter totals it gains abilities and becomes a creature.,Tap another creature you control: Put charge counters equal to its power on this Spacecraft. Station only as a sorcery. It's an artifact creature at N+.,forge_oracle,,
  Warp,keyword,702.185,Starbreach Whale,Written as Warp [cost]. Cast the card from hand for its warp cost; exile it at the next end step and it can be cast again from exile on a later turn.,"You may cast this card from your hand for its warp cost. Exile this creature at the beginning of the next end step, then you may cast it from exile on a later turn.",printed,,
  ∞ (Infinity),keyword,702.186,702.186,"∞ (the mathematical symbol for infinity) is a keyword found on Infinity cards. ""∞"" is followed by ability text. Together, they represent a static ability.","∞ (the mathematical symbol for infinity) is a keyword found on Infinity cards. ""∞"" is followed by ability text. Together, they represent a static ability.",cr_rule_702.186a,,
  Mayhem,keyword,702.187,702.187,Mayhem is a static ability that functions while the card with mayhem is in a player's graveyard.,You may cast this card from your graveyard for {C}{C} if you discarded it this turn. Timing rules still apply.,printed,,
  Web-slinging,keyword,702.188,702.188,"Web-slinging is a static ability that functions while the spell with web-slinging is on the stack. ""Web-slinging [cost]"" means ""You may cast this spell by paying [cost] and returning a tapped creature you control to its owner's hand rather than paying its mana cost."" Casting a spell using its web-sl",You may cast this spell for {C}{C} if you also return a tapped creature you control to its owner's hand.,printed,,
  Firebending,keyword,702.189,702.189,"Firebending is a triggered ability. ""Firebending N"" means ""Whenever this creature attacks, add N {R}. Until end of combat, you don't lose this mana as steps and phases end.""","Whenever this creature attacks, add {C}. This mana lasts until end of combat.",printed,,
  Sneak,keyword,702.190,702.190,"Sneak is a keyword that represents a static ability that functions while the spell with sneak is on the stack. ""Sneak [cost]"" means ""Any time you could cast an instant during your declare blockers step, you may cast this spell by paying [cost] and returning an unblocked creature you control to its o",You may cast this spell for {C}{C} if you also return an unblocked attacker you control to hand during the declare blockers step.,printed,,
  Increment,keyword,702.191,702.191,"Increment is a triggered ability. ""Increment"" means ""Whenever you cast a spell, if this permanent is a creature and the amount of mana spent to cast that spell is greater than this creature's power or this creature's toughness, put a +1/+1 counter on this creature.""","Whenever you cast a spell, if the amount of mana you spent is greater than this creature's power or toughness, put a +N/+N counter on this creature.",printed,,
  Paradigm,keyword,702.192,702.192,"Paradigm represents two spell abilities, one of which creates a delayed triggered ability. Paradigm means ""If this is the first time a spell you control with this spell's name has resolved this game, at the beginning of each of your precombat main phases for the rest of the game, create a copy of th","Then exile this spell. After you first resolve a spell with this name, you may cast a copy of it from exile without paying its mana cost at the beginning of each of your first main phases.",printed,,
  Power-up,keyword,702.193,702.193,"Power-up is a keyword that adds additional rules to the activated ability that follows it. ""Power-up — [Cost]: [Effect]"" means ""[Cost]: [Effect]. If this permanent entered this turn, this ability's cost is reduced by this permanent's mana cost. Activate this ability only once.""","Power-up is a keyword that adds additional rules to the activated ability that follows it. ""Power-up - [Cost]: [Effect]"" means ""[Cost]: [Effect]. If this permanent entered this turn, this ability's cost is reduced by this permanent's mana cost. Activate this ability only once.""",cr_rule_702.193a,,
  Teamwork,keyword,702.194,702.194,"Teamwork represents a static ability that functions while the spell with teamwork is on the stack. ""Teamwork N"" means ""As an additional cost to cast this spell, you may tap any number of creatures you control with total power N or more."" Paying a spell's teamwork cost follows the rules for paying ad","As an additional cost to cast this spell, you may tap any number of creatures you control with total power N or more.",printed,,
  Storied,keyword,702.195,Balin Loremaster,If you control three or more artifacts / legendary permanents / Sagas (any mix) you have an enduring story for the rest of the game; some Storied cards act differently once you do.,"If you control three or more artifacts, legendaries, and/or Sagas, you have an enduring story for the rest of the game.",forge_oracle,,
  Regeneration,action,,Ancient Silverback,"Written as ""regenerate: [cost]"" When the regeneration cost is paid, it gives that permanent a ""regeneration shield"" for the rest of the turn.",,no_cr_rule,,
  Tap/untap,action,,,Allows you to tap or untap a permanent.,,no_cr_rule,,
  Adventure,keyword,,Bonecrusher Giant,"On a card with adventure, you may cast a spell for it's adventure cost. If you do, exile that card. You may then cast the creature side from exile. You have to cast adventure spell, then creature half. You cannot cast creature half, then adventure from exile.",,no_cr_rule,,
  Alliance,keyword,,Gala Greeters,"Basically ""Landfall"", but on creatures. Whenever another creature enters, some effect happens.",,no_cr_rule,2022-04-29,24
  Bloodrush,keyword,,Skarrg Goliath,"Written as ""Bloodrush [cost]"" You may discard a creature with bloodrush by paying its bloodrush cost. Then, a target creature is granted a boost and abilities based off the discarded creature.",,no_cr_rule,2013-02-01,13
  Channel,keyword,,Greater Tanuki,"Written as ""Channel [cost]"" You may pay the channel cost of a card in your hand, if you do, you discard that card and yield some effect.",,no_cr_rule,2005-06-03,39
  Coven,keyword,,Augur of Autumn,"If you control at least 3 creatures with different powers, then creatures with coven gain some benefit.",,no_cr_rule,2021-09-24,20
  Daybound/Nightbound,keyword,,Brutal Cathar,"The day/night cycle must be introduced by a card with daybound/nightbound. Whenever a player plays 2 or more spells on their turn, it becomes day. If a player casts no spells during their turn, it becomes night. Cards with this mechanic transform or give some",,no_cr_rule,2021-09-24,73
  Fabricated,keyword,,Angel of Invention,"Written as ""Fabricate X"", where X is a number Whenever a creature with fabricate enters the battlefield, you may either put X +1/+1 counters on that creature or create X 1/1 colorless servo creature tokens.",,no_cr_rule,,
  Flip,keyword,,"Erayo, Soratami Ascendant","Flip cards are turned upside-down when a certain condition is met. They are not turned face-down, but rotated 180 degrees.","Cards Cards with a two-part card frame (one part of which is printed upside down) on a single card. See rule 710, ""Flip Cards.""",cr_glossary,,
  Imprint,keyword,,Extraplanar Lens,"Written as ""Imprint [something]"" When a card with imprint enters the battlefield, it can have you exile almost anything, then gives you some boon based on that.","""Imprint"" used to be a keyword ability. It is now an ability word and has no rules meaning. All cards printed with the imprint keyword have received errata in the Oracle card reference.",cr_glossary,2003-10-02,30
  Inspired,keyword,,"King Macar, the Gold-Cursed","Whenever a card with inspired becomes untapped, something happens.",,no_cr_rule,2014-02-07,19
  Jump-start,keyword,702.133,Radical Idea,Cards with Jump-start may be cast from the graveyard by paying their mana cost and discarding a card.,You may cast this card from your graveyard by discarding a card in addition to paying its other costs. Then exile this card.,printed,2018-10-05,13
  Level up,keyword,702.87,Lighthouse Chronologist,"Cards with level up enter the battlefield at level 0. You may pay the level up cost to put a level counter on that creature. As creatures ""gain experience (level up)"", they gain more abilities. You may only level up as a sorcery, but may do so as many times as",{C}: Put a level counter on this. Level up only as a sorcery.,printed,2010-04-23,26
  Morph and Megamorph,keyword,,Ainok Survivalist,"Written as ""Morph [cost]"" You may pay 3 generic mana and put a card with morph onto the battlefield face down as a colorless 2/2 creature. Then you may pay the morph cost to flip the card face up.",,no_cr_rule,2002-10-07,184
  Totem Armor,keyword,,Bear Umbra,"Totem Armor is only on auras. If a creature attached with an aura that has Totem Armor would die, instead, the aura is destroyed instead.","(Obsolete) An obsolete keyword ability that has been renamed. See rule 702.89, ""Umbra Armor.""",cr_glossary,,
  Addendum,ability_word,,Emergency Powers,Cards with addendum have an added effect if cast in your main phase.,,no_cr_rule_ability_word,2019-01-25,10
  Battalion,ability_word,,Legion Loyalist,Creatures with battalion have an additional effect trigger if they attack with at least 2 other creatures,,no_cr_rule_ability_word,2013-02-01,22
  Chroma,ability_word,,Fiery Bombardment,"Cards with chroma check for specific mana symbols in specific zones, then give a benefit or effect based on that.",,no_cr_rule_ability_word,2008-07-25,9
  Domain,ability_word,,Prismatic Geoscope,"Cards with domain have some effect related to the number of basic land types you control. Some good effects, some bad effects.",,no_cr_rule_ability_word,2000-10-02,58
  Enrage,ability_word,,Ranging Raptors,"Only on creatures. If a creature with enrage is dealt damage, some type of trigger will occur.",,no_cr_rule_ability_word,2017-09-29,25
  Fateful Hour,ability_word,,Break of Day,Cards with fateful hour gain an additional ability if it's controller is at 5 or less life.,,no_cr_rule_ability_word,2012-02-03,10
  Ferocious,ability_word,,Wild Slash,Cards with ferocious gain an additional ability if their controller also controls a creature with more than 4 power.,,no_cr_rule_ability_word,2014-09-26,26
  Grandeur,ability_word,,"Baru, Fist of Krosa",Very few cards with this and they are bad. Allows you to discard a card with the same name to give it a bonus.,,no_cr_rule_ability_word,2007-05-04,7
  Hellbent,ability_word,,Infernal Tutor,"Cards with hellbent give some additional boon or greater effect if you have no cards in hand when the card resolves. If you cast the card, and while it is on the stack, you somehow discard your hand, you will still get the hellbent ability even though you had",,no_cr_rule_ability_word,2003-01-01,23
  Heroic,ability_word,,Fabled Hero,Cards with heroic grant some additional benefit when targeted with a spell.,,no_cr_rule_ability_word,2013-09-27,45
  Join forces,ability_word,,Collective Voyage,Cards with join forces allow all players to contribute mana towards some effect. Meant for commander/multiplayer games.,,no_cr_rule_ability_word,2011-06-17,5
  Kinship,ability_word,,Pyroclast Consul,"On your upkeep, if you control a card with kinship, you may look at the top card of your library. If it is a creature that shares a type with the kinship creature on the battlefield, you may reveal it for some effect.",,no_cr_rule_ability_word,2008-02-01,12
  Landfall,ability_word,,Khalni Heart Expedition,Cards with landfall have some ability that triggers when a land enters the battlefield.,,no_cr_rule_ability_word,2005-10-07,197
  Metalcraft,ability_word,,Puresteel Paladin,Cards with metalcraft gain an additional benefit if it's controller controls 3 or more artifacts.,,no_cr_rule_ability_word,2010-10-01,35
  Morbid,ability_word,,Tragic Slip,Cards with morbid gain some effect if a creature died that turn.,,no_cr_rule_ability_word,2011-09-30,29
  Radiance,ability_word,,Rally the Righteous,"Basically, if you target a permanent with a spell, that spell affects all permanents of the same type that share a color. If you have 5 white creatures and cast Rally the Righteous on one, the other 4 with also get +3/+3",,no_cr_rule_ability_word,2005-10-07,10
  Raid,ability_word,,Bloodsoaked Champion,Cards with raid get some effect if their controller attacked before playing them.,,no_cr_rule_ability_word,2014-09-26,46
  Rally,ability_word,,Lantern Scout,Cards with rally have some effect trigger whenever a creature with the type Ally enters the battlefield.,,no_cr_rule_ability_word,2015-10-02,14
  Sweep,ability_word,,Charge Across the Araba,"When you cast a spell with sweep, you may return any number of lands with the basic land type as dictated by the card. Some effect is gained from this. Not a good mechanic.",,no_cr_rule_ability_word,2005-06-03,4
  Threshold,ability_word,,Nimble Mongoose,Cards with threshold gain some effect when you have 7 or more cards in the graveyard.,"""Threshold"" used to be a keyword ability. It is now an ability word and has no rules meaning. All cards printed with the threshold keyword have received errata in the Oracle card reference.",cr_glossary,2001-10-01,108
  Undergrowth,ability_word,,Kraul Foragers,Cards with undergrowth have effects dependent on the amount of creatures in your graveyard.,,no_cr_rule_ability_word,2018-10-05,13
  Chapter,keyword,,,Chapter abilities are the numbered abilities on a Saga. A lore counter is added each turn after the first main phase draw step and each chapter triggers when counters reach its number; the Saga is sacrificed after the last chapter.,"As this Saga enters and after your draw step, add a lore counter. Sacrifice after III.",forge_oracle,,
  Class,keyword,,,Class enchantments have levels. Pay each level's cost at sorcery timing in order to unlock that level's ability; levels are permanent while the Class stays on the battlefield.,"An enchantment subtype. Classes have a number of class level abilities that increase their level and grant them new abilities. See rule 716, ""Class Cards.""",cr_glossary,,
  Choose a Background,keyword,,Halsin Emerald Archdruid,Commander rule keyword. Lets the commander have a Background enchantment as a second commander.,You can have a Background as a second commander.,forge_oracle,,
